      "anchors": [
        {
          "before": "The social effects of these improvements depend on how people organize and use technology;\nthey are not automatically guaranteed by a political system or by technological development itself.",
          "after": "Physics is an important foundation of modern natural science.\nThe laws it investigates and the instruments it develops influence many fields of research, technology and production.\nExamples from astronomy, the life sciences, energy and electronics illustrate these connections."
        },
        {
          "before": "Physics is an important foundation of modern natural science.\nThe laws it investigates and the instruments it develops influence many fields of research, technology and production.\nExamples from astronomy, the life sciences, energy and electronics illustrate these connections.",
          "after": "For thousands of years, astronomical observations relied mainly on visible light, which occupies only a small part of the electromagnetic spectrum.\nAdvances in radio physics made radio astronomy another means of observation and broadened our understanding of the universe."
        },
        {
          "before": "This does not mean that every kind of particle and radiation can already be observed.\nThese observations have greatly expanded astronomy's sources of information, with an important contribution from detection methods and recording instruments developed in physics.\nCombining astronomy with physics allows astrophysics to investigate the properties and processes of celestial objects more deeply.",
          "after": "Molecular biology and genetics investigate the molecular basis of life processes and the transmission and action of genetic information.\nMolecules are material components of living systems, not tiny organisms that live independently."
        },
        {
          "before": "Theories and experimental methods from physics also help chemistry, geology, oceanography and other natural sciences investigate the properties of matter and natural processes.\nTheir development illustrates how different sciences support one another.",
          "after": "Physics also provides a scientific foundation for many technological developments.\nEnergy engineering, communication, transport, construction and industrial and agricultural production can use physical laws and research findings to improve equipment and processes.\nSuch improvements also require contributions from other disciplines and engineering practice."
        },
        {
          "before": "Nuclear physics provides a scientific foundation for both fission and fusion energy.\nPractical power systems also need support from other fields of physics and engineering.",
          "after": "**Modern technology can use materials whose properties are designed for particular purposes**, but these materials still require material feedstocks and do not eliminate the use of natural resources.\nMaterial synthesis and processing allow properties to be adjusted to technological needs."
        },
        {
          "before": "Physical methods using electron beams, ion beams, laser beams, strong magnetic fields, high pressure, high temperature and ultrasound can be combined with chemical methods to prepare or treat suitable materials.\nThey can produce particular material properties and new ways of processing materials, thereby improving production processes.",
          "after": "Many production processes in industry and agriculture can be automated.\nAutomated systems measure the state of a process and use electronic controls to adjust equipment operation."
        },
        {
          "before": "These steps produce devices with particular structures and electrical functions.\nThey cannot simply be described as layers of a particular kind of molecule.\nMiniaturization can put part of a radio's circuitry on a chip the size of a match head, but the chip is not a complete radio with its antenna, power supply and other components.",
          "after": "These examples do not cover every influence of physics on science and technology, but they show its close connections with many fields. **Modern physics has made important contributions to scientific and technological development**, working together with other disciplines and engineering practice."
        }
      ],
